  "question": {
    "text": "Metal deficiency defect is shown by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>93</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. In the crystal, some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> cations are missing and loss of positive charge is compensated by the presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions. The percentage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions in the<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>93</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> crystals is____(Nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "85",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>93</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> for every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>93</mn><mi>Fe</mi></math> ions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>93</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>79</mn></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ions</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>%</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>79</mn><mn>93</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> nearest integer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>",
